logic-cut
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: the operator's ask after direct-once: `Logic.once` (the Prolog
  cut) becomes `Logic.cut`, so `once` in this library means one thing
  (`!.once`, the Once effect) and a file importing both `!.*` and
  `Logic.*` is not ambiguous. Code, the one caller (okay-agent
  Search.bestOf), and every prose mention of the cut; the scoped-
  effects literature's `once` in theory ch. 5 is the paper's word and
  stays.
files: src/main/scala/Logic.scala, src/test/scala/TestLogic.scala,
  okay-agent/src/main/scala/okay/agent/Search.scala, docs/{guide,tutorial,typepedia,direct-style}.md,
  docs/theory/07-logic-streams.md, docs/modules/okay-agent.md,
